====1F (Lower)====
=====Let There Be Light=====
Speak to the Hiker near the entrance, and he warns that it will be difficult to navigate the darker parts of the cave. He mentions how he saw a man named [[Steven Stone|Steven]] earlier who was able to use {{m|Flash}}, and should be alright on his own. As you are unable to do so, the Hiker gives you your own copy of {{HM|05|Flash}}.

Continue westward through the chamber to reach an [[Escape Rope]], then climb down the nearby ladder.

====B1F====
Head north from the ladder, then turn eastward. Pick up the {{i|Poké Ball}} in the first dead-end path to the south, then climb down the ladder to the southeast.

====B2F====
Go west and climb the stairway to reach the upper level. Turn eastward and climb up the northeast ladder.

====B1F====
Climb up the next ladder to return to 1F.

====1F (Upper)====
Follow the path westward and enter the chamber at its end.

====1F (Back)====
Speak to the man in the rear chamber, and he introduces himself as [[Steven Stone|Steven]]. He is interested in rare stones, and travels all around looking for more to add to his collection. Steven soon realizes that you have a [[Letter]] for him, and accepts the delivery. As thanks, he gives you a TM that contains his favorite move, {{TM|47|Steel Wing}}. Seeing your capable-looking Pokémon, he encourages you to keep up your training so that you might become the Pokémon Champion one day. He then exits the chamber.
{{-}}
==Dewford Town==
Speak to [[Mr. Briney]] at the pier. There is still another delivery to be made, so it is time to set sail for [[Slateport City]].

==Routes 107 and 108==
[[File:Hoenn Route 107 RS.png|thumb|left|200px|Route 107]]
[[File:Hoenn Route 108 RS.png|thumb|200px|Route 108]]

As [[Mr. Briney]] again sails directly to the next destination, there is no chance to fully explore the waters of Routes {{rtn|107|Hoenn}} and {{rtn|108|Hoenn}} on the first visit. There is little of interest on Route 107, but Route 108 holds the remains of a half-sunken [[Abandoned Ship]].



